# Default-deny inbound.
#
# Two ways in, both authenticated and both restricted by source:
#   eth0  192.168.1.0/24   the local LAN
#   tun0  10.99.0.0/24     the management VPN (second layer of defence)
#
# Outbound is unrestricted: lnd needs it for Mutinynet neutrino filters, for
# Lightning peer connections, and for the VPN itself.
#
# Deliberately NOT opened:
#   10009/tcp  lnd gRPC   - admin macaroon is full control, use lncli over SSH
#   8080/tcp   lnd REST   - same
#   7000/tcp   lndk gRPC  - same, use lndk-cli over SSH
#   9735/tcp from the LAN or the internet. Lightning p2p is reachable over the
#            VPN only, which is how the server opens the channel to us.

*filter
:INPUT DROP [0:0]
:FORWARD DROP [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]

-A INPUT -i lo -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -m conntrack --ctstate INVALID -j DROP

# --- LAN (eth0) -----------------------------------------------------------
-A INPUT -i eth0 -s 192.168.1.0/24 -p tcp --dport 22 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -i eth0 -s 192.168.1.0/24 -p icmp --icmp-type echo-request -j ACCEPT

# --- Management VPN (tun0) ------------------------------------------------
# SSH over the tunnel is the second path in, independent of the LAN.
-A INPUT -i tun0 -s 10.99.0.0/24 -p tcp --dport 22 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# Lightning p2p, so the server node at 10.99.0.1 can dial us and open a channel.
-A INPUT -i tun0 -s 10.99.0.0/24 -p tcp --dport 9735 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# LNURL-pay. The gateway holds the public name and certificate and proxies to
# this port over the tunnel, so a customer's wallet can fetch a payRequest
# from a device that accepts no inbound connection from the internet.
-A INPUT -i tun0 -s 10.99.0.0/24 -p tcp --dport 8090 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -i tun0 -s 10.99.0.0/24 -p icmp --icmp-type echo-request -j ACCEPT

COMMIT
